                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A charming game.\n\nI like the visual style, the game-play feels good, and overall little details, like the goblin sweating when you hang on the platform or a little bunny appearing behind a snow hill are awesome. Feels like a game made by a real person with passion for what they were doing. Each location has a unique vibe, the goblin has his own character and the simple story bits are great as well.\n\nHowever I don't like the lives system, because in this game you'll die a lot, and losing all lives means you have to start again or go through a punishing dungeon without your upgrades. I'm not sure if I'll continue because even though I'd like to see the whole game, I don't want to get stressed about losing my progress every time I lose a life.\n",
